chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "Bitcoin Security"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the book's own source at tag third_edition_print1. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-10-15T13:47:12Z; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.4." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P17, chx:P18, chx:P19, chx:P20, chx:P21, chx:P22, chx:P23, chx:P24, chx:P25, chx:P26, chx:P27, chx:P28, chx:P29, chx:P30, chx:P31, chx:P32, chx:P33, chx:P34, chx:P35, chx:P36, chx:P37, chx:P38, chx:P39, chx:P40, chx:P41, chx:P42, chx:P43, chx:P44, chx:P45, chx:P46, chx:P47, chx:P48, chx:P49, chx:P50, chx:P51, chx:P52, chx:P53, chx:P54, chx:P55, chx:P56, chx:P57, chx:P58, chx:P59, chx:P60, chx:P61, chx:P62, chx:P63, chx:P64, chx:P65, chx:P66, chx:P67, chx:P68, chx:P69, chx:P70, chx:P71, chx:P72, chx:P73, chx:P74, chx:P76, chx:P75, chx:P77 .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "What does Chapter 13 of Mastering Bitcoin (3rd edition) say about the security model of Bitcoin, the root of trust, the protection of keys by cold storage, hardware signing devices and encryption, the backup that keeps access, the sharing of control by multisignature and the survival of access after the key holder, which of its statements can be recomputed or run on Bitcoin Core 31.1 and against published test vectors, and what has changed in Bitcoin Core, the BIPs and the history of custody since the book went to print?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-10-15." .
